  "success": true,
  "output": "Here's the full performance analysis with actionable fixes:\n\n---\n\n## Performance Analysis\n\n### 1. N+1 Query Patterns\n\n**1.1 — `callTitle()` called inside a loop** (`apps/api/src/websocket/calls.ts:227`)\n\n`callTitle()` issues 1–2 DB queries per call, and it's called inside a `for...of` loop over invitees. For a 5-person call, that's 10 redundant queries for the same event/conversation.\n\n```typescript\n// ❌ Current: N queries for N invitees\nfor (const userId of await invitees(call, user.id)) {\n  emitToUsers([userId], \"call:incoming\", {\n    title: await callTitle(call, userId), // DB hit per iteration\n  });\n}\n\n// ✅ Fix: fetch once, broadcast to all\nconst title = await callTitle(call, user.id); // one query\nfor (const userId of await invitees(call, user.id)) {\n  emitToUsers([userId], \"call:incoming\", { title });\n}\n```\n\n**1.2 — `invitees()` called twice per call lifecycle** (`apps/api/src/websocket/calls.ts:116,227`)\n\nThe same attendee/member query runs once to check if the user can end the call, then again to broadcast. Cache it in the handler scope.\n\n**1.3 — `registerPresence()` makes 3 separate queries** (`apps/api/src/websocket/presence.ts:9–27`)\n\nTwo queries run upfront (memberships + group memberships), then a third fetches visible users from the same `member` table. Combine the last query with the first using `include`:\n\n```typescript\n// ✅ Single query with includes\nconst members = await db.member.findMany({\n  where: { userId: user.id },\n  include: { organization: { include: { members: { include: { user: true } } } } },\n});\n```\n\n---\n\n### 2. Unnecessary Re-renders\n\n**2.1 — `PollWidget` creates new `Map`/`Set` on every render** (`apps/web/src/components/feed/poll-widget.tsx:31–43`)\n\n```typescript\n// ❌ Current: recalculated every render\nconst counts = new Map(poll.options.map((o) => [...]))\nconst voters = new Set(poll.votes.map((v) => v.userId))\n\n// ✅ Fix: memoize\nconst { counts, voters } = useMemo(() => ({\n  counts: new Map(poll.options.map((o) => [...])),\n  voters: new Set(poll.votes.map((v) => v.userId)),\n}), [poll.options, poll.votes, pending]);\n```\n\n**2.2 — `repliesOf()` filters entire array per comment** (`apps/web/src/components/feed/comments-thread.tsx:58–60`)\n\nWith 10 comments + replies, the array is filtered 10+ times per render:\n\n```typescript\n// ❌ Current: O(n) filter per comment\nconst repliesOf = (id: string) => (comments ?? []).filter((c) => c.parentId === id)\n\n// ✅ Fix: group once\nconst repliesMap = useMemo(() => {\n  const m = new Map<string, typeof comments>();\n  for (const c of comments ?? []) {\n    if (c.parentId) {\n      const arr = m.get(c.parentId) ?? [];\n      arr.push(c);\n      m.set(c.parentId, arr);\n    }\n  }\n  return m;\n}, [comments]);\n```\n\n**2.3 — `ConversationList` O(n×m) filter runs every render** (`apps/web/src/components/chat/conversation-list.tsx:49–66`)\n\nThe member-name search iterates every conversation × every member on each keystroke and on unrelated re-renders. Wrap in `useMemo([rows, q])`.\n\n**2.4 — `ReactionSummary` recomputes counts Map on every render** (`apps/web/src/components/feed/reactions.tsx:227–229`)\n\nA feed with 50 posts triggers 50+ Map rebuilds per render. Wrap in `useMemo([reactions])`.\n\n---\n\n### 3. Caching Opportunities\n\n**3.1 — Org/member data uses 30s `staleTime`** (`apps/web/src/components/layout/org-layout.tsx:49–60`)\n\nMember roles rarely change mid-session. Increase:\n\n```typescript\n// In the member useDbQuery call:\n{ staleTime: 10 * 60_000 } // 10 minutes instead of 30 seconds\n```\n\nApply the same to sidebar group membership queries (`apps/web/src/components/layout/app-sidebar.tsx:84–101`).\n\n**3.2 — `useRealtimeSync` invalidates too broadly** (`apps/web/src/hooks/use-realtime-sync.ts:13–45`)\n\n`\"post:changed\"` invalidates the entire `[\"post\"]` key, wiping out pagination and causing full refetches for a single post edit:\n\n```typescript\n// ❌ Current: nukes all post queries\nqueryClient.invalidateQueries({ queryKey: [\"post\"] })\n\n// ✅ Fix: invalidate only the affected entity\nqueryClient.invalidateQueries({ queryKey: [\"post\", event.data.id] })\n```\n\n**3.3 — No route prefetching on navigation**\n\nAdd prefetch on link hover for the most common transitions (group feed, chat list) to eliminate loading spinners:\n\n```typescript\n// In nav links:\nonMouseEnter={() => queryClient.prefetchQuery(groupPostsQuery(groupId))}\n```\n\n---\n\n### 4. Memory Leaks\n\n**4.1 — `live` Map and `answered` Set grow without eviction** (`apps/api/src/websocket/calls.ts:23–25`)\n\nIf `endCall()` is never reached (crash, client disconnect without cleanup), call state leaks forever. Add a TTL-based eviction:\n\n```typescript\n// After storing a call:\nsetTimeout(() => {\n  if (live.has(callId)) {\n    endCall(callId, db); // force-end stale calls\n  }\n}, 24 * 60 * 60 * 1000);\n```\n\n**4.2 — Hub room Map retains empty Sets** (`apps/api/src/websocket/hub.ts:34–86`)\n\nThe `dispose()` path checks `size === 0` before deletion — verify this path runs reliably under load and that no other code path bypasses it. Add a periodic scan for stale empty rooms as a safety net.\n\n---\n\n### 5. Redundant Computations\n\n**5.1 — `sameGroup()` called 3–4× per message** (`apps/web/src/components/chat/message-list.tsx:166–175`)\n\nEach message checks grouping with the previous and next message using `differenceInMinutes` (expensive). Precompute grouping once:\n\n```typescript\nconst grouped = useMemo(() =>\n  messages.map((msg, i) => ({\n    ...msg,\n    isGrouped: sameGroup(messages[i - 1], msg),\n    isGroupedNext: sameGroup(msg, messages[i + 1]),\n  })),\n[messages]);\n```\n\n**5.2 — `dayLabel()` reformats the same date strings repeatedly** (`apps/web/src/components/chat/message-list.tsx:39–48`)\n\nCache with a `Map` inside `useMemo`:\n\n```typescript\nconst dayLabels = useMemo(() => {\n  const cache = new Map<string, string>();\n  return (date: Date) => {\n    const key = format(date, \"yyyy-MM-dd\");\n    if (!cache.has(key)) cache.set(key, dayLabel(date));\n    return cache.get(key)!;\n  };\n}, []);\n```\n\n---\n\n### Priority Order\n\n| Priority | Issue | Impact |\n|---|---|---|\n| 🔴 High | N+1 in `callTitle()` loop | Every call, multiplied by participants |\n| 🔴 High | Broad cache invalidation in `useRealtimeSync` | All feeds, every mutation |\n| 🟠 Medium | `PollWidget` / `ReactionSummary` inline Maps | Every feed render |\n| 🟠 Medium | `registerPresence()` 3-query sequence | Every WebSocket connect |\n| 🟡 Low | `staleTime` tuning for org/member data | Steady-state query pressure |\n| 🟡 Low | `live` Map TTL eviction | Long-running server stability |\n\nThe two highest-impact changes to ship first are the **`callTitle()` query hoisting** (server-side, zero UI risk) and the **granular `useRealtimeSync` invalidation** (reduces feed refetch churn significantly).\n",
